From 1bcfd67c49d846bcf1571ded27569341afc4d13f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Hartkopp <socketcan@hartkopp.net>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 20:33:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/32] can: isotp: drop frames without N_PCI

isotp_rcv() reads the address extension and the N_PCI without checking
the CAN frame data length. So frames with CAN_DL < ae + N_PCI_SZ are
processed with stale data beyond CAN_DL, e.g. as SF, CF or FC.

Drop these frames as they are no valid N_PDUs. This also ensures that
datalen - pcilen in isotp_rcv_sf() can not underflow.

Fixes: e057dd3fc20f ("can: add ISO 15765-2:2016 transport protocol")
Signed-off-by: Oliver Hartkopp <socketcan@hartkopp.net>
---
 net/can/isotp/protocolrx.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/can/isotp/protocolrx.c b/net/can/isotp/protocolrx.c
index 730d889..794f2b9 100644
--- a/net/can/isotp/protocolrx.c
+++ b/net/can/isotp/protocolrx.c
@@ -510,6 +510,10 @@ void isotp_rcv(struct sk_buff *skb, void *skdata)
 	if (!data)
 		return;
 
+	/* frames without N_PCI (and AE) are no N_PDUs */
+	if (datalen < ae + N_PCI_SZ)
+		return;
+
 	/* if enabled: check reception of my configured extended address */
 	if (ae && *(data) != so->opt.rx_ext_address)
 		return;
